From: Lars <118484383+LarzVader@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: aic: ignore a scan confirm after the scan was aborted

rwnx_close() aborts a running scan: it reports it to cfg80211, drops the
scan activity reference and clears scan_request, then cancels the scan in
the firmware. The firmware still sends SCANU_START_CFM afterwards, and
without CONFIG_AIC8800_SCHED_SCAN the handler calls cfg80211_scan_done()
unconditionally, i.e. with NULL. That oopses in the RX thread (seen when
NetworkManager bounces the interface to change the MAC address) and the
device stops working. Return early when no scan is pending.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
@@ -686,6 +686,17 @@
 
 	RWNX_DBG(RWNX_FN_ENTRY_STR);
 
+	/*
+	 * The confirm can arrive after the scan was finished elsewhere, e.g.
+	 * aborted in rwnx_close() (scan_request cleared, scan activity
+	 * released there). Reporting it again would pass NULL to
+	 * cfg80211_scan_done() and drop the activity reference twice.
+	 */
+	if (!rwnx_hw->scan_request) {
+		rwnx_hw->scanning = 0;
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 #ifdef CONFIG_AIC8800_SCHED_SCAN
 	if (rwnx_hw->scan_request && !rwnx_hw->is_sched_scan)
 #endif // CONFIG_AIC8800_SCHED_SCAN
